ThermoGuard AI — How to Run and Test
ThermoGuard AI is an AI-based industrial fire detection system that uses satellite fire data and a YOLO-based AI model to identify possible fire and smoke events.
1. Requirements
Install:
Python 3.10+
Node.js 18+
Git
A modern web browser
2. Download the Project
Clone the GitHub repository:
git clone YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
cd Thermo-Guard-AI
3. Set Up the Backend
Open a terminal inside the project folder:
cd backend
pip install -r requirements.txt
Add the AI model
Place the trained best.pt file inside:
backend/
└── best.pt
The trained model file is required for AI image detection.
Add NASA FIRMS API Key
Create:
backend/.env
Add:
NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY=YOUR_NASA_FIRMS_KEY
Each user should use their own NASA FIRMS key.
4. Start the Backend
Inside the backend folder:
uvicorn main:app --reload
The backend will normally run at:
http://127.0.0.1:8000
Open this in a browser to check that the API is running.
5. Set Up the Frontend
Open another terminal and go back to the main project folder:
cd ..
npm install
Create a file:
.env
Add:
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
VITE_DEMO_MODE=false
6. Start the Frontend
Run:
npm run dev
Open the URL shown in the terminal, usually:
http://localhost:5173
7. How to Test ThermoGuard AI
🔥 AI Image Detection
Open AI Analysis.
Upload a suitable fire/smoke image.
Provide the location if required.
Start the analysis.
The AI model detects Fire / Smoke / No Detection.
The system displays the detection confidence and prototype risk level.
🛰️ Satellite Monitoring
Open Satellite Monitoring.
View available NASA FIRMS fire observations.
Check fire locations on the map.
Select an incident to view its information.
🗺️ Fire Map
Open Fire Map to view detected incidents and their locations geographically.
🚨 Alerts
Open Alerts to view fire events classified by the prototype risk rules.
📜 History
Open History to view previous detection results.
